WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.599 --> 00:00:07.859
When stepping back and thinking about it,
it is kind of odd that as the human species,

00:00:07.859 --> 00:00:12.650
we take possession of other types of species
and call them our pets.

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:21.250
And it is even odder that it is accepted as
normal across essentially all of humanity.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:26.990
We take animals that cannot communicate with
us on any real coherent level, bring them

00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:32.029
into our homes, call them our pets, and live
with them.

00:00:32.029 --> 00:00:36.329
We feed them, shelter them, and take care
of them.

00:00:36.329 --> 00:00:42.550
And generally, all we ask in return is that
we just get to be around them.

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:43.649
But why is this?

00:00:43.649 --> 00:00:49.469
What is so appealing about sharing our life
with another species like a dog, cat, bird,

00:00:49.469 --> 00:00:50.469
fish, hamster, etc.?

00:00:50.469 --> 00:00:57.219
Outside of more practical reasons like assisting
in hunting, gathering, general tasks, etc.,

00:00:57.219 --> 00:01:05.150
one reason for assimilating pets is the human
desire to have responsibility and control.

00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:06.780
The need to feel important.

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:12.170
And the need to feel like something is dependent
on us.

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:18.820
This feeling is empowering, and as humans,
our central insecurities are partly satiated

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:25.439
by the sense of superiority we experience
when owning and domesticating another living

00:01:25.439 --> 00:01:27.530
being.

00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:33.880
On the surface, this might sound somewhat
feeble and selfish of us humans, but the truth

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:40.759
is, although this may be a motive, there is
a much deeper and more sincere reason why

00:01:40.759 --> 00:01:44.140
we like owning and being around our pets.

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:51.950
A reason that makes the relationship between
human and animal companion a truly mutual,

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:58.780
interdependent, and beautiful one that reveals
a wonderful side of our nature.

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:01.539
We do not simply own our pets.

00:02:01.539 --> 00:02:03.090
We love them.

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:10.770
We become best friends with them and form
bonds that are truly reciprocal and unconditional.

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:17.550
We give them access to consistent safety,
health, comfort, and other logistical things

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:21.000
that they might struggle to sustain.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:27.590
And in return, they help remind us of a side
of ourselves that we want so deeply to live

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:30.580
in, but often struggle with.

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:33.800
The appreciation for simplicity.

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:36.520
The ability to feel free.

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:39.200
The obsession with fun.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:42.680
The lack of sensitivity to embarrassment.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:46.200
The disinterest in holding grudges.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:51.870
And the unrestrained affection that our pets
possess are all of the things that we long

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:59.490
for and wish we could feel constantly in ourselves,
but often struggle to do so.

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:05.950
And our pets embody and remind us of the importance
and possibility of these things.

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:12.230
I would argue that the elements of our nature
that our pets lack, like complex language,

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:19.950
logical understanding, heightened self awareness,
etc. are all equally beautiful and essential

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:24.650
to what makes the human experience so uniquely
wonderful.

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:31.750
But I would also argue that it can be very
easy to become lost in this part of ourselves.

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:35.720
The part that needs to understand and control
everything.

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:42.180
And our animal companions help show us that
we don’t always need to.

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:48.470
That life can sometimes be best enjoyed by
simply enjoying it for what it is.

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:49.470
Feeling it.

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:50.470
Playing in it.

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:52.290
Rolling in its grass.

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:58.150
And so perhaps at the end of the day, even
though we may like to think that our pets

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:28.540
depend on us, it may be more so the other
way around.

